      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m a bit worried about the 1KB that `spans[64]` and `slots[64]` put on the stack. This frame stays live while GUP faults the pages in, which can enter direct reclaim, on top of the filesystem frames of every O_DIRECT read or write in a 4KB process. aosp/4312497 avoided that by taking `slots` from the unused tail of `pages`.\n\nWould a smaller cap, e.g. 16 entries (256 bytes, 64KB per GUP call), work as well?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "72d7aab9ef20860431890b05dd677fa70b2e0ae2",
